#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443409} :activity/id #uuid "93b447e0-191c-560c-ac25-bc9695d12742" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048143 :topic/id #uuid "82e1668e-936b-52f4-a230-dc0cb3dc1f13" :topic/math-academy-id 3133} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443409 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443406 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d08e6f7-0c8c-5a19-bed7-db8dc41af65e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443350} {:answer/id #uuid "7e31c437-06d1-5826-9cb1-4684802533dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443354} {:answer/id #uuid "89017994-b329-5175-a753-3bf33a611163" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443358} {:answer/id #uuid "c6c810b0-869e-5ce1-8f1a-3a1e0dbb11d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443367} {:answer/id #uuid "dd9ebd11-88f5-552e-b5e4-2988eb8b37a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443377}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443377} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c8bfdef-6f81-5a7f-8190-7d981c16e459" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443393}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "77278df4-e113-5900-8941-27a77a33d7c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-98696" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the $3$rd column of the matrix $U?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if  $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of a $3\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n- $Σ$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix with nonnegative elements on the main diagonal and zeroes outside the main diagonal,\n\n- $U$ is an orthogonal $3\\times 3$ matrix,\n\n- $V$ is an orthogonal $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=3$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=1.$\nAlso, the columns ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ of $V$ give us the right singular vectors of $A.$\n\nTherefore, we can compute the $1$st and $2$nd columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we do not have the third singular value, we can't use the same formula to find the third column of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal. Hence, we must find a vector \n\n$$\n{u}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nsuch that \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0,\\end{aligned}\\,‖{u}_{3}‖=1.\n$$\n\nSolving this system, which is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}{x}_{1}-\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{2}}{x}_{2}-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{x}_{1}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe get the nonzero normalized solution \n\n$$\n{u}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrix $U:$\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "46bb3e49-3990-5b69-ab08-fafc145eef1c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443411}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443410 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443407 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "521d6dc6-c306-5eff-a662-c8d5ca209cac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{x}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443340} {:answer/id #uuid "5a1282dd-cff4-5d9d-aea1-997f77fae849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2{x}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443343} {:answer/id #uuid "e6ac364e-730c-5977-844b-64abc957eff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443381}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443343} :answer-field/id #uuid "01393794-e39b-5872-af64-efa4c600b9fc" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443388} {